  "rationale": "Booker Little's defining studio statement as a leader: a sextet date cut over two sessions in spring 1961 for Nat Hentoff's Candid label, all seven compositions by Little himself (S1). Consensus evidence is strong and independently tabulated at S1: AllMusic 5 stars (Scott Yanow's review, also at S3), The Rolling Stone Jazz Record Guide 5 stars, The Penguin Guide to Jazz Recordings 3.5 stars, and Pitchfork 9.3/10. Session gravity is the case for the canon: Eric Dolphy on alto saxophone, bass clarinet and flute, Julian Priester on trombone, Don Friedman on piano, Art Davis or Ron Carter on bass, and Max Roach on drums, timpani and vibes (S1, S2, S4). Little died at 23 later in 1961; this is the fullest document of a composer-bandleader whose writing bridges hard bop and the coming avant-garde.",
