    "notes": "Two sessions at Nola Penthouse Sound Studios, New York City (S2, S4): March 17, 1961 (We Speak; Quiet Please; A New Day — Art Davis, bass) and April 4, 1961 (Strength and Sanity; Moods in Free Time; Man of Words; Hazy Hues — Ron Carter, bass). All seven compositions by Booker Little (S1). Producer/supervisor Nat Hentoff (S1, S2). No engineer is documented in the sources consulted, so `engineer` is null rather than inferred. Original issue Candid CJM 8027 (mono); also CJS 9027, Barnaby BR-5019 (1977), Candid CCD 79027 (S2, S4)."
